# Visual Basic quick start

The same first script in Visual Basic. With `kind: Statements` you write the statements only;
Invoklet puts them inside a `Module` with a `Sub Main` for you.

Press **Run** (F5) and look at the **Results** tab under the editor.

```vb run
Dim languages = {"C#", "Visual Basic"}
Console.WriteLine($"Hello from Invoklet! {languages.Length} languages are supported.")

languages.
    Select(Function(name, index) New With {.Position = index + 1, .Name = name, .Letters = name.Length}).
    Dump("Supported languages")
```

`.Dump()` works the same in both languages: it renders any value, here a collection of
anonymous objects, as a table.
